  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600142",
      "title": "Exploring The Core Redux Concepts",
      "sourceHash": "24af37eed7d76b8647b311ae2cc1c470e628cb7dae87be367430f1449c0d28fe",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 4.93,
          "en": "Now for exploring the Redux basics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.93,
          "end": 6.71,
          "en": "I have a brand new project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.71,
          "end": 10.43,
          "en": "and this isn't even a React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.43,
          "end": 12.22,
          "en": "It's an empty folder in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.22,
          "end": 15.21,
          "en": "just have some settings for my IDE here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "Now you can therefore also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 18.88,
          "en": "just create a brand new empty folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.88,
          "end": 21.85,
          "en": "We don't need a React App yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.85,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "of course, we will add one later, but for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 27.05,
          "en": "an empty folder we'll do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.05,
          "end": 32.05,
          "en": "And in that folder, you can create a new JavaScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.05,
          "end": 33.65,
          "en": "You can give it any name you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.65,
          "end": 37.093,
          "en": "I will name it Redux-demo.JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.93,
          "end": 41.78,
          "en": "Now we will execute this file with node JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.78,
          "end": 45.13,
          "en": "because node JS allows us to run JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.13,
          "end": 47.57,
          "en": "outside of the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.57,
          "end": 50.74,
          "en": "And of course, we already have node JS installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.74,
          "end": 53.29,
          "en": "because we needed that for creating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.29,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "our react apps for installing our third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 61.61,
          "en": "with NPM and also for running our development server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.61,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "So we already do have node JS installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 70.43,
          "en": "And now here, in this empty folder, I will run NPM in it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.57,
          "end": 73.21000000000001,
          "en": "and you should do this too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.21000000000001,
          "end": 75.64,
          "en": "Open a terminal or a command prompt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.64,
          "end": 77.83,
          "en": "navigate into this empty folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.83,
          "end": 82.293,
          "en": "and run NPM in it to be precise, run NPM in it -y,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 87.2,
          "en": "which simply answers all these default questions with yes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.2,
          "end": 89.41,
          "en": "if you don't run it with -y,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.41,
          "end": 91.963,
          "en": "just answer them manually with yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.87,
          "end": 95.3,
          "en": "Now this gives us a package.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.3,
          "end": 97.46000000000001,
          "en": "which is not too interesting for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.46000000000001,
          "end": 101.00999999999999,
          "en": "but we need it to install third-party packages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.00999999999999,
          "end": 103.963,
          "en": "Because now we wanna install Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.82,
          "end": 109.4,
          "en": "For this we can now run NPM install Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.4,
          "end": 112.50999999999999,
          "en": "That's the name of that package and when we run this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.50999999999999,
          "end": 115.16,
          "en": "this package gets installed into this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.16,
          "end": 117.72,
          "en": "otherwise empty project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 120.16,
          "en": "We therefore node modules folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.16,
          "end": 124.51,
          "en": "which now contains Redux and all the dependencies of Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.51,
          "end": 127.18,
          "en": "Now we're ready to use Redux here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.18,
          "end": 131.52,
          "en": "So in the Redux-demo.js file, we can now use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "Now for that we need to import Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "And since we were going to execute this file with node JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 141.72,
          "en": "the import will look a little bit different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.72,
          "end": 144.19,
          "en": "than what we're used to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.19,
          "end": 147.79,
          "en": "We import Redux like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.79,
          "end": 149.2,
          "en": "This might look strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.2,
          "end": 152.82,
          "en": "but that is the default node JS import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 155.91,
          "en": "for importing a third party package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.91,
          "end": 160.91,
          "en": "And we import Redux from the Redux package with this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.32999999999998,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "Now we need to do a couple of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 169.22,
          "en": "If you recall that slide, we will need to create that store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.29,
          "end": 173.62,
          "en": "we will need to create a reducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.62,
          "end": 177.9,
          "en": "which changes that store, we will then also need an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.9,
          "end": 182.78,
          "en": "and a component or since we're not using a React app yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.78,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "any other code that sets up a subscription to the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 190.57,
          "en": "So I think it makes sense to start with the store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.57,
          "end": 194.783,
          "en": "since that is the central piece and concept of Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 197.92000000000002,
          "en": "Now we can create such a store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.92000000000002,
          "end": 200.92000000000002,
          "en": "by using that imported Redux object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.92000000000002,
          "end": 204.59,
          "en": "And then on that object, we can call, createStore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.59,
          "end": 207.93,
          "en": "That's a method exposed by the Redux library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.93,
          "end": 211.53300000000002,
          "en": "which does what the name implies, it creates a store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.68,
          "end": 215.82,
          "en": "Now let's store that store in a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.82,
          "end": 218.95,
          "en": "which you of course don't have to name store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.95,
          "end": 220.92000000000002,
          "en": "but I think it's a name that makes sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.92000000000002,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "given that we create a store here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 226.65,
          "en": "And then the question is, how do we proceed?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.65,
          "end": 229,
          "en": "What do we do with that store?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229,
          "end": 232.24,
          "en": "Well, that store should manage some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.24,
          "end": 235.53,
          "en": "and the data which it manages is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.53,
          "end": 238.04,
          "en": "determined by the reducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.04,
          "end": 241.64,
          "en": "because it's the reducer function which will produce",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.64,
          "end": 243.88,
          "en": "new state snapshots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.88,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "The reducer has to go of spitting out a new state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.06,
          "end": 251.59,
          "en": "whenever an action reaches it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.59,
          "end": 254.61,
          "en": "And when we run this code for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.61,
          "end": 258.74,
          "en": "the reducer will also be executed with a default action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.74,
          "end": 262.39,
          "en": "so to say, that should spit out the initial state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.39,
          "end": 264.6,
          "en": "So therefore the next thing we need to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.6,
          "end": 266.86,
          "en": "is a reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.86,
          "end": 270.54,
          "en": "And I will name this counter reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.54,
          "end": 273.933,
          "en": "but the name is up to you, and that stores a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.97,
          "end": 278.32,
          "en": "Here I'm using this anonymous arrow function syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.32,
          "end": 283.1,
          "en": "Of course you could also create that function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.1,
          "end": 284.78,
          "en": "That would also be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.78,
          "end": 287,
          "en": "But I'll stick to the Arbor syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287,
          "end": 290.25,
          "en": "And that's now our reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 292.25,
          "en": "It's not finished though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.25,
          "end": 296.86,
          "en": "A reducer function is a standard JavaScript function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.86,
          "end": 301.01,
          "en": "but it will it be called by the Redux library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.01,
          "end": 304.7,
          "en": "and it will then always receive two pieces of input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.7,
          "end": 309.05,
          "en": "two parameters, the old or existing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.05,
          "end": 312.16,
          "en": "and the action that was dispatched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.16,
          "end": 317.12,
          "en": "And then this reducer function must return a certain output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 317.12,
          "end": 322.05,
          "en": "It must always return a new state object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 322.05,
          "end": 326.14,
          "en": "And therefore a reducer function should be a pure function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 326.14,
          "end": 328.49,
          "en": "Which basically means that the same inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 328.49,
          "end": 332.65999999999997,
          "en": "the same values for inputs always should produce",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.65999999999997,
          "end": 334.81,
          "en": "exactly the same output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 334.81,
          "end": 339.23,
          "en": "And there should be no side effects inside of that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 339.23,
          "end": 342.76,
          "en": "So you must not send a HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 342.76,
          "end": 345.49,
          "en": "or write something to local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 345.49,
          "end": 348.75,
          "en": "or fetch something from local storage there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 348.75,
          "end": 352.24,
          "en": "Instead, a reducer should really just be a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 352.24,
          "end": 356.26,
          "en": "that takes the given inputs, which are provided by Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 356.26,
          "end": 361.023,
          "en": "and then produces the expected output, a new state object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 362.24,
          "end": 364.04,
          "en": "So therefore back in code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 364.04,
          "end": 367.76,
          "en": "this reducer function will receive the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 367.76,
          "end": 371.16,
          "en": "the current state and the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 371.16,
          "end": 373.26,
          "en": "It receives that by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 373.26,
          "end": 376.62,
          "en": "because the reducer will ultimately be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 376.62,
          "end": 378.96,
          "en": "by the Redux library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 378.96,
          "end": 382.5,
          "en": "And then we should return the new state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 382.5,
          "end": 385.78,
          "en": "which will replace the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 385.78,
          "end": 386.98,
          "en": "Now here on the slide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 386.98,
          "end": 390.41,
          "en": "I said that the output is a state object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 390.41,
          "end": 393.78,
          "en": "it typically will be because in most applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 393.78,
          "end": 397.07,
          "en": "state is more than just one single of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 397.07,
          "end": 401.23,
          "en": "but theoretically, it can be any kind of value type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 401.23,
          "end": 404.44,
          "en": "State can also just be a number or a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 404.44,
          "end": 408.42,
          "en": "But in reality, it will most often be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 408.42,
          "end": 411.64,
          "en": "So here we then wanna return, let's say a new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 412.52,
          "end": 416.86,
          "en": "and then this object can have any structure we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 416.86,
          "end": 421.01,
          "en": "This is totally up to us, the developer of this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 421.01,
          "end": 424.21,
          "en": "So here we could have a counter field in this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 424.21,
          "end": 427.29,
          "en": "which is zero for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 427.29,
          "end": 430.3,
          "en": "Now this word user would always return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 430.3,
          "end": 432.79,
          "en": "with a counter set to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 432.79,
          "end": 435.56,
          "en": "Now that might not be too realistic though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 435.56,
          "end": 438.18,
          "en": "Instead, the counter should probably be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 438.18,
          "end": 440.72,
          "en": "the existing counter and then let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 440.72,
          "end": 443.38,
          "en": "the existing counter plus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 443.38,
          "end": 448.08,
